<head>
<no><b>Part 1</b></no><heading guid="_1c34fba0-7451-4418-a326-69f63cefb98f"
id="pt.1-he"><b>Preliminary</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ae65835e-38b0-4735-8edd-81c60013d8cd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_4d56c4fe-d583-497b-89e1-19db50c01e7a"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref type="act" jurisd="NSW"
check="unknown" refid="act-2012-058"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Fiscal
Responsibility Act 2012</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_90d0415b-7abd-47f8-8eca-796fbd124461"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_5d5ff00b-0fd3-4cf7-b9d1-88e769538ab1"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on the date of assent to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_150aa225-fbd4-469b-a9f9-ad6b02a1286a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_8a231a66-7744-4207-be9e-f9f12ac5256c"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Object of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_abaa4e75-1596-4400-8538-2b36709208b7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The object of this Act is to maintain the AAA
credit rating of the State of New South Wales.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_07cc1f8a-0ca7-4c6b-8914-b57253413bf5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The purpose of that object is&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_86ab5ebf-acb7-4c9a-bb2c-3185c91c7984" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to limit the cost of government borrowing,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_33c082a9-a9e7-49d2-8f8d-02ee3b632e1d" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to enable access to the broadest possible
investor base for government borrowing, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f4412da2-31e1-49e3-bff9-edafed8fa10a" id="sec.3-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to maintain business and consumer confidence,
thereby sustaining economic activity and employment in the
State.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_45b8bb19-5d52-4cba-9440-a312c2b658bb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_01ef8ca3-56e5-4e42-a9b2-b657decaf5a1"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Application of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act applies to and in respect of the State
budget.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bc0fa476-24a4-4e4e-8064-6a41c48c4d3b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_4adfccbb-5571-48bb-aedd-e7b47a4d1d09"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6e3a11fd-6de2-4466-bc76-f68b911c1842"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_cc38de72-0418-49f7-8c23-3f65a48abb62"
id="sec.5-def.budgetpapers"><b><i>budget papers</i></b></defterm> means the
budget papers of the Government tabled in Parliament in connection with the
annual Appropriation Bills.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_8e99ca3e-f3f0-4f95-a4c5-a32f52c4e5e1"
id="sec.5-def.longtermaveragegeneralgovernmentrevenuegrowth"><b><i>long-term
average general government revenue growth</i></b></defterm> of the State means
the average annual growth rate of general government revenue over a
sufficiently long previous period to smooth out the influence of transient
factors. The regulations may prescribe the relevant rate.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_2c47adcf-4ee5-4449-b340-208cb1581314"
id="sec.5-def.longtermfiscalgap"><b><i>long-term fiscal gap</i></b></defterm>
means the change in the primary balance of the general government sector as a
share of gross state product, calculated on the basis of no policy
changes&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_48288779-5021-4ab3-94a9-702e9a541250" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">from 2009&#8211;10 to 2050&#8211;51,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3d2cb363-26eb-4d7a-8ef4-908fddcab7dc" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">after a re-assessment under section 8&#8212;over
a similar sufficiently long period to assess fiscal pressures associated with
the ageing population and other long-term trends. The regulations may
prescribe the relevant period.</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">For the purpose of this definition, the <defterm
type="definition" guid="_585844d6-daad-4d37-909a-3ab2115e73c2"
id="sec.5-def.primarybalance"><b><i>primary balance</i></b></defterm> is
revenue less expenditure, including net capital expenditure but not including
interest transactions.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_3ef044c8-0172-40bb-904e-54fd133ad541"
id="sec.5-def.theStatesunfundedsuperannuationliability"><b><i>the
State&#8217;s unfunded superannuation liability</i></b></defterm> means the
total net employer liabilities of the State under defined benefit
superannuation schemes for the total state sector.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ae200625-88ee-483c-8236-3d2c57b03f31"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Expressions used in this Act (to the extent they
are not otherwise defined in this Act) have the same meaning as similar
expressions used by the Australian Bureau of Statistics in the preparation of
government finance statistics.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4ce216b0-2049-466e-b3d8-8717db9c46e3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Notes included in this Act do not form part of
this Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e6e0b6f8-b785-4292-a284-0f2e355d9db8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_47bf899e-2582-44fc-8cec-bb8c0205a996"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Fiscal targets and principles</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7c808e52-5c5a-4b47-b715-3aeebf58d504"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_59673a63-77fa-4d46-9231-5a18145c4673"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Fiscal targets</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The fiscal targets for achieving the object of
this Act are as follows&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0ed54360-648a-4827-8581-f97344e04d2d" id="sec.6-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">The annual growth in general government expenses
of the State is less than the long-term average general government revenue
growth of the State.</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2a3d8fe9-3ad0-4214-b3ed-a67f309c9bfd" id="sec.6-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">The elimination of the State&#8217;s unfunded
superannuation liability by 2030.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ba94b4ba-56a6-4d24-9e22-302b0e3d17c1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_8b8ef2ce-3559-4de3-9f96-a980e00ed6d4"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Principles of sound financial
management</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_53ae569b-6f67-485f-b25a-587e06f5ed97"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The policy objectives of the Government should be
pursued in accordance with the principles of sound financial management set
out in this section in order to support the object of this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_28fbb7be-f9d3-44ca-a562-2f71c12c61f6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Principle No 1 is responsible and sustainable
spending, taxation and infrastructure investment, including&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8f86632b-f7d8-412a-a8fc-2b2590c466ec" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">aligning general government revenue and expense
growth, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_598bcd87-5dcc-469b-bec3-972e2ea9797b" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">stable and predictable taxation policies,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ef6580f1-8be6-4b6b-b19b-e2f14a4aec78" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">investment in infrastructure that has the highest
benefit for the community.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a6d877d1-867c-4cf4-b468-a415770170d4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Principle No 2 is effective financial and asset
management, including sound policies and processes for&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ff8d8534-d130-4d1b-9f3f-e2e4c4d7240b" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">performance management and reporting,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c79ccd53-cc88-4892-b49b-6dee6428a571" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">asset maintenance and enhancement,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_75da087b-0372-4d23-b5c7-dd06375fe2c9" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">funding decisions, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f5a48a0f-56ba-4e06-a673-de1f798bc987" id="sec.7-ssec.3-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">risk management
practices.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0d613c4b-c5c4-4fb1-a527-f2f7017f6a6e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Principle No 3 is achieving intergenerational
equity, including ensuring that&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_adaab9c7-783d-4606-8a82-7f9c4aec7adf" id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">policy decisions are made having regard to their
financial effects on future generations, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_08c27ef2-e42b-4b5d-90fd-5a88a1c791b3" id="sec.7-ssec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the current generation funds the cost of its
services.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e71cb649-3bd9-43a7-a031-3321c0bcf59b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_9d183d86-7101-4727-b0a0-b333a7194442"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Budget reporting in relation to fiscal targets and
principles</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Treasurer is to include the following in the
budget papers&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f098ef37-f49d-4fa2-a42f-593f4cded51e" id="sec.8-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a statement of the Government&#8217;s fiscal
strategy having regard to the object of this Act and the fiscal targets and
principles provided by this Act,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_54549a02-97de-4492-bfbb-850a92e68014" id="sec.8-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a report on the Government&#8217;s performance
against that object and those targets and principles,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7de918d7-14ff-4652-b147-283eb46415b9" id="sec.8-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the reasons for any departure from that object
and those targets and principles, together with the action planned to achieve
that object and those targets and principles within the forward years of the
budget,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4c6d6088-ef9f-4a31-bdf3-463b6077b8a9" id="sec.8-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an assessment of the impact of the measures in
the budget on the State&#8217;s long-term fiscal gap,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_cc46b0ef-201e-4f7b-9a90-936147f3cf47" id="sec.8-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in the case of the budget papers for
2016&#8211;17 and for each 5 years thereafter&#8212;an updated report on
long-term fiscal pressures and a re-assessment of the State&#8217;s long-term
fiscal gap.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<note type="legtext" guid="_a9653bbd-ba69-431b-872b-4ec4c0c47967"
id="sec.8-note"><heading guid="_7af7dcd2-ea24-4c42-aae0-7a6882981d86"
id="sec.8-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">Section 10 of the <legref type="act" jurisd="NSW"
check="unknown" refid="act-2002-060"><name emphasis="yes"><i>General
Government Liability Management Fund Act 2002</i></name></legref> requires the
Management Committee (constituted under that Act to advise the Secretary of
the Treasury on the management of the Fund) to review from time to time the
long-term fiscal target of eliminating total State sector unfunded
superannuation liabilities by 2030.</txt></block></note>
</level>
</level>


